            <div xml:id="d508">

                <pb facs="0593" n="500" sameAs="frus:frus1935v04/pg500"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">339.115 General Motors Export Co./147:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in the Dominican Republic</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Schoenfeld</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Santo
                                Domingo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-05-18T11:00:00-05:00">May 18, 1935—11
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received 1:45 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>67. Tour telegram No. 26, May 17, 5 p.m. I am delivering note to Foreign Office
                    this morning in the sense of your instruction and I am stating on the basis of
                    information supplied to me by vice president of Dominican Tobacco Company that
                    American interests in the Company are evidently sustaining injury as a result of
                    continued imprisonment of the Company’s president.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Schoenfeld</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
